// SF32 miniboard reference - intentionally disabled for fabrication.
//
// The original design instantiated several contrib parts before their pin and
// footprint evidence had been audited. The audit found that:
//
// - SF32LB52X and BHI260AP lack complete manufacturer PCB-land evidence;
// - CH343P lacks a manufacturer-recommended QFN land pattern;
// - the formerly selected RT9080 part/variant was incompatible with its
//   device model (the library has since been corrected, but this board has not
//   been re-reviewed);
// - the former MicroSD and SX1262 data were unsafe (their library definitions
//   are corrected now, but the complete board has not been re-reviewed).
//
// Consequently the old BOM, netlist, footprints, design lock, and KiCad
// schematic were removed. This empty top keeps the package checkable while
// making its reference-only status explicit. Re-enable a real design only
// after every instantiated part has an audited purchasable binding.

design SF32MiniBoardReference {
}
